$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM A solution of ketone 29 (20 mg, 0.032 mmol), phenethylamine chlorohydride
(50 mg, 0.245 mmol, 7.6 equiv) and soldium acetate (26 mg, 0.322 mmol, 10
equiv) in anhydrous ethanol (3 ml) was stirred at 23 °C for 3 hours. The
reaction mixture was diluted with ethyl acetate (50 ml) and filtered. The
filtrate was concentrated and the residue was purified by flash column
chromatography (50% EtOAc in heptane) to afford ecteinascidin 770 (24 mg,
97%) as a white film. [α]D24.5 -50.6 °(c = 0.7, CHCl3). IR (neat film) ν
3434, 2932, 1742, 1588, 1508, 1453, 1369, 1327, 1235, 1106, 1086, 1053,
1028, 959 cm-1 ; 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 6.59 (s, 1H), 6.46 (s, 1H),
