$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Representative experimental procedure for a
thiourea- and BzOH-catalyzed enantioselective iso-Pictet-Spengler
reaction of isotryptamine 2a and aldehyde 3n: (Isobutyraldehyde (3n) was
purified immediately prior to use by distillation over CaSO4. Stock
solution of benzoic acid (0.50 M in toluene) was prepared.) Isotryptamine
2a (16.0 mg, 0.100 mmol, 1.00 equiv.), chiral thiourea 5b (12.8 mg,
0.0200 mmol, 0.200 equiv.), and toluene (2 mL) were added into an
oven-dried 2-dram vial charged with a stir bar. Then, a solution of
benzoic acid in toluene (20.0 uL, 0.0100 mmol, 0.100 equiv.) and
isobutyraldehyde 3n (10.0 uL, 0.110 mmol, 1.10 equiv.) were added by
syringes and the resulting heterogeneous solution was allowed to stir for
1 hour at 22 °C.
(S)-1-(4-Chlorophenyl)-1-methyl-2,3,4,5-tetrahydro-1H-pyrido[4,3-b]indole
(8), yield 95%. IR (neat): 3396 (w), 3142 (w), 3053 (w), 2928 (w), 1585
(w), 1486 (m), 1455 (s), 1426 (m), 1397 (w), 1369 (w), 1323 (m), 1207
(m), 1182 (m), 1011 (s) cm-1; 1H NMR (CDCl3, 500 MHz): δ 8.02 (1H, br s),
7.38-7.36 (3H, m), 7.29-7.28 (1H, m), 7.23 (2H, d, J = 8.2 Hz), 7.17 (1H,
t, J = 7.6 Hz), 7.07-7.04 (1H, m), 3.21- 3.16 (1H, m), 2.91-2.84 (2H, m),
2.72-2.68 (1H, m), 1.92 (3H, s), 1.88 (1H, br s); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 125
MHz): δ 146.3, 135.8, 133.4, 132.6, 128.9, 128.3, 126.4, 121.5, 120.3,
119.8, 115.7, 111.0, 57.4, 39.3, 29.8, 24.8; LRMS (ESI+): Calcd for
C18H18ClN2 [M+H]: 297.1, found: 297.1. Specific Rotation: [α ]D24 -83.7
(c 1.45, CH2Cl2).
