$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Large Scale Synthesis of Compound 7d. To a solution of
2-(1H-indole-1-yl)ethanamine 3 (1.32 g, 8.20 mmol, 1.05 equiv.) in 50 mL
of benzene was added ketoamide 4d (1.77 g, 7.80 mmol, 1.0 equiv.) and the
solution was heated at reflux using a Dean-Stark apparatus for 16 hours.
The solution was then cooled to room temperature and the Dean-Stark
apparatus was replaced with a septum. A solution of silane (S,S)- 1 (3.10
g, 10 mmol, 1.3 equiv.) in benzene (4.0 mL) was added and the mixture was
heated to reflux until the reaction was completed after 8h. The reaction
mixture was then cooled to room temperature, quenched by the addition of
H2O (50 mL) and stirred for 30 min. The aqueous phase was separated and
extracted with EtOAc (4*70 mL). The combined organic phase was washed
with saturated aqueous NaHCO3 (50 mL) and brine (50 mL). It was dried
over anhydrous Na2SO4, filtered and concentrated. The residue was
recrystallized from hexanes/chloroform. 2.72 g (94% yield), pale yellow
crystalline solid. The enantiomeric excess of the product was determined
to be 98% by comparison to a sample of the racemate. [α]22 = 15.0 (c =
1.2, CHCl3). 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.44 (bs, 1H, NH-CO), 7.66 (d, J=
7.6 Hz, 1H, Ar-H), 7.35 (d, J= 7.9 Hz, 1H, Ar-H), 7.26 - 7.13 (m, 4H,
Ar-H), 6.94 (t, J= 8.0 Hz, 2H, Ar-H), 6.71 (s, 1H, Ar-H), 4.22 (m, 1H,
N-CH2), 4.01 (td, J= 11.0, 4.6 Hz, 1H, N-CH2), 3.39 (m, 2H, NH-CH2), 2.18
(dtd, J= 25.6, 13.9, 4.8 Hz, 2H, CH2), 1.51 (m, 2H, NH-CH2), 0.98 (t, J=
7.3 Hz, 3H, CH3). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 173.1, 159.9 (d, J= 5.0 Hz),
156.5(d, J= 3.8 Hz), 136.6, 135.9, 128.2 (m), 122.0, 121.1, 120.7, 114.2,
112.2, 111.9, 109.4, 101.9, 100.0, 64.8, 43.2, 42.7, 41.0, 17.8, 14.7. IR
(thin film) 3309, 2961, 2925, 2866, 1695, 1513, 1452,1361, 1239, 1176,
1013, 779, 741. LRMS for C21H21F2N3O (FAB+): calcd. 370.18 ([M+H]+),
found 370.20 ([M+H]+).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Dean-Stark apparatus used (stage 1), 98% ee,
iso-Pictet-Spengler reaction, scalable,multigram scale, alternative
reaction conditions gave lower yield and stereoselectivity
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Direct and highly enantioselective iso-Pictet-Spengler reactions with
α-ketoamides: Access to underexplored indole core structures
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Schonherr, Heike; Leighton, James L.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2012), 14(10), 2610-2613

