$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a solution of 27 (54 mg, 0.06 mmol, 1.0 equiv) in 11.4 mL anhydrous
THF at 0 °C was added TBAF (1.0 M in THF, 125 µL, 0.12 mmol, 2.2 equiv)
over ca. 30 sec. The mixture was stirred 10 min, after which MsOH (92 µL,
1.4 mmol, 25 equiv) was added rapidly in one portion by syringe. The
resulting mixture was stirred for 10 min, after which the reaction was
quenched with 15 mL saturated aq NaHCO3 and was then diluted with 20 mL
EtOAc. The resulting layers were separated and the aq phase was extracted
with 2 x 15 mL EtOAc. The combined organic phases were dried (Na2SO4),
filtered, and concentrated. The crude product was chromatographed on
silica gel (EtOAc) to give 28 as an amorphous white powder (30 mg, 0.05
mmol, 89%). Recrystallization of 28 in chloroform-pentane using the vapor
diffusion method afforded clear, needle-like crystals suitable for X-ray
analysis. [α]25D: + 28.5 (c 1.0, CH2Cl2). IR (thin film): 2936, 2856,
1636 cm-1. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 6.06 (dddd, J = 17.0, 10.4, 5.8,
5.8 Hz, 1H), 5.94 (app dd, J = 8.1, 3.2 Hz, 1H), 5.50 (s, 1H), 5.34 (app
dd, J = 17.0, 1.3 Hz, 1H), 5.31-5.24 (m, 2H), 4.86-4.77 (m, 2H), 4.50
(1/2 ABX, JAB = 10.9 Hz, 1H), 4.47 (1/2 ABX, JAB = 12.4 Hz, 1H), 4.02
(app s, 1H), 3.85 (app dd, J = 11.7, 3.8 Hz, 1H), 3.77-3.70 (m, 1H), 3.73
(s, 3H), 3.72 (s, 3H), 3.69 (s, 3H), 3.64 (s, 3H), 3.60-3.49 (m, 2H),
3.48-3.38 (m, 2H), 3.26-3.15 (m, 1H), 3.06-2.97 (m, 2H), 2.82 (app d, J =
17.9 Hz, 1H), 2.40 (s, 3H), 2.19 (s, 3H), 2.16 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (100 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 169.6, 152.7, 150.0, 149.5, 145.2, 143.8, 142.7, 135.1, 134.4,
125.5, 124.9, 124.2, 122.6, 122.5, 118.8, 117.8, 116.3, 73.8, 71.7, 70.3,
61.0, 60.4, 60.3, 60.0, 59.3, 55.2, 54.3, 49.0, 39.8, 28.9, 19.7, 9.7,
9.6. TLC (SiO2, 100% EtOAc): Rf= 0.41. Mp: 203-204 °C. HRMS (FAB+) calcd
for C33H43N2O8 (m/z) 595.3019; found (m/z) 595.3026.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
