$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Method B. 5 A solution of isatin (1.0 mmol), tryptamine (1.0 mmol) and
1,3-bis(3,5- bis(trifluoromethyl)phenyl)thiourea or Sc(OTf)3 (0.1 mmol,
20 mol %) was prepared in dry CH2Cl2 (0.06 M) at 25 °C in an oven-dried
and Ar-purged 4 mL vial containing a magnetic stir bar. The reaction was
stirred until it was complete as judged by TLC (80% EtOAc/hexanes). The
reaction was then concentrated and loaded onto a flash silica gel column
(gradient of EtOAc/hexanes ending in 80% EtOAc/hexanes). The
spiroindolone product. Table 2, entry 1:
6'-methoxy-1-(prop-2-ynyl)-2',3',4',9'-tetrahydrospiro[indoline-3,1'-pyrido[3,4-b]indol]-2-one
(16a): The general method B for the addition of 5-methoxytryptamines was
used with Sc(OTf)3. Beige solid (yield 86 mg, 89% yield). 1H NMR (400
MHz, DMSO) δ 9.36 (s, 1H), 6.54 (m, 1H), 6.35 (m, 1H), 6.30 (m, 1H), 6.24
- 6.14 (m, 2H), 6.11 (s, 1H), 5.84 - 5.80 (m, 1H), 3.78 (dd, J = 17.8,
1.3, 1H), 3.58 (dd, J = 17.8, J = 1.1, 1H), 2.90 (s, 3H), 2.72 (m, 1H),
2.27 (m, 1H), 2.16, (s, 1H), 2.00 - 1.83 (m, 2H), 1.65 (dd, J = 1.3, J =
1.1, 1H); LRMS (ESI) m/z [M + H]+ calcd for C22H20N3O2, 358.15 ; found
358.3; XlogP = 2.73.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, stereoselective, alternative thiourea-derivative catalyst
gave lower yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Catalytic Stereoselective Synthesis of Diverse Oxindoles and
Spirooxindoles from Isatins
