$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: D) General Procedure for the
Iso-Pictet-Spengler Reaction to synthesize
Tetrahydropyrazino[1,2-a]indoles 7. To a solution of the indole 3 (0.315
mmol, 1.05 equiv.) in 3.0 mL of toluene was added the ketoamide 4 (0.30
mmol, 1.0 equiv.), and the solution was heated at reflux using a
Dean-Stark apparatus for 16 hours. The solution was then cooled to room
temperature and the Dean-Stark apparatus was replaced with a septum. A
solution of silane (S,S)-1 (0.45 mmol, 1.5 equiv.) in toluene (2.0 mL)
was added and the mixture was heated to reflux until the reaction was
completed (monitored by TLC hexanes:ethyl acetate 1:1). The reaction
mixture was then cooled to room temperature and quenched by the addition
of MeOH (0.5 mL). The mixture was concentrated and the residue was
purified by flash chromatography. According to the general procedure for
the synthesis of tetrahydropyrazino[1,2-a]indoles the title compound 7i
was isolated by flash chromatography (5:1 to 1:1 hexanes : ethyl acetate)
in 89% yield. The enantiomeric excess of the product was determined to be
92% by comparison to a sample of the racemate. Time 5 h. [α]22 = 8.7 (c =
0.5, CHCl3). 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.42 (bs, 1H, NH-CO), 7.66 (d, J=
7.7 Hz, 1H, Ar-H), 7.35 (d, J= 7.9 Hz, 1H, Ar-H), 7.20 (m, 4H, Ar-H),
6.94 (t, J= 8.1 Hz, 2H, Ar-H), 6.70 (s, 1H, Ar-H), 4.22 (m, 1H, N-CH2),
4.02 (td, J= 10.9, 4.5 Hz, 1H, N- CH2), 3.44 (m, 1H, NH-CH2), 3.32 (m,
1H, NH-CH2), 2.63 (s, 1H, NH), 2.17 (m, 2H, CH2), 1.55 (m, 2H, CH2), 1.26
(m, 27H, CH2), 0.90 (t, J= 6.6 Hz, 3H, CH3). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ
173.2, 136.7, 135.9, 128.2, 122.0,121.1, 120.6, 112.2, 111.9, 109.4,
100.0, 64.8, 42.7, 41.0, 32.3, 30.2, 29.8, 29.9, 30.1, 24.4, 23.1, 14.5.
IR (thin film) 3311, 3050, 2924, 2852, 1698, 1596, 1512, 1455, 1361,
1241, 1014, 778, 743. LRMS for C32H43F2N3O (FAB+): calcd. 524.34
([M+H]+), found 524.19 ([M+H]+).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Dean-Stark apparatus used (stage 1), 92% ee,
iso-Pictet-Spengler reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Direct and highly enantioselective iso-Pictet-Spengler reactions with
α-ketoamides: Access to underexplored indole core structures
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Schonherr, Heike; Leighton, James L.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2012), 14(10), 2610-2613

