$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: C) General Procedure for the
Iso-Pictet-Spengler Reaction to synthesize Pyrrolo[4,3,2-
de]isoquinolines 6. To a solution of (1H-Indol-4-yl)methanamine 2 (0.315
mmol, 1.05 equiv.) in 3.0 mL of benzene was added the ketoamide 4 (0.30
mmol, 1.0 equiv.), and the solution was heated at reflux using a
Dean-Stark apparatus for 16 hours. The solution was then cooled to room
temperature and the Dean-Stark apparatus was replaced with a septum. A
solution of silane (S,S)-1 (0.45 mmol, 1.5 equiv.) in benzene (2.0 mL)
was added and the mixture was heated to reflux until the reaction was
completed (monitored by TLC hexanes:ethyl acetate 1:1). The reaction
mixture was then cooled to room temperature and quenched by the addition
of MeOH (0.5 mL). The mixture was concentrated and the residue was
purified by flash chromatography. According to the general procedure for
the synthesis of pyrrolo[4,3,2-de] isoquinolines the title compound 6f
was isolated by flash chromatography (6:1 to 1:1 hexanes : ethyl acetate)
in 87% yield. The enantiomeric excess of the product was determined to be
98% by comparison to a sample of the racemate. Time 8 h. [α]22 =-9.9 (c =
1.0, CHCl3). 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 9.03 (bs, 1H, NH-CO), 8.21 b(s,
1H, NH), 7.18 (m, 4H, Ar-H), 6.94 (t, J= 8.1 Hz, 2H, Ar-H), 6.89 (d, J=
6.7 Hz, 1H, Ar-H), 4.32 (s, 2H, NH- CH2), 2.28 (dd, J= 13.5, 5.0 Hz, 1H,
CH2), 2.00 (ddd, J= 17.8, 13.4, 6.2 Hz, 3H, CH2, CH , CH2- NH), 1.02 (t,
J= 6.5 Hz, 3H, CH3). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 173.3, 159.9, 156.5,
133.8, 129.2, 127.6 (t, J= 9.8 Hz), 124.8, 122.9, 120.1, 114.8, 114.6,
113.9, 112.2, 111.9, 109.3, 63.7, 49.1, 43.9, 25.1, 24.9, 24.9. IR (thin
film) 3369, 2954, 2910, 2862, 1684, 1608, 1512, 1454, 1237, 1012, 752.
LRMS for C21H21F2N3O (FAB+): calcd. 370.18 ([M+H]+), found 370.15
([M+H]+).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Dean-Stark apparatus used (stage 1), 98% ee,
iso-Pictet-Spengler reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Direct and highly enantioselective iso-Pictet-Spengler reactions with
α-ketoamides: Access to underexplored indole core structures
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Schonherr, Heike; Leighton, James L.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2012), 14(10), 2610-2613

