$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the synthesis of
pyrrolo[2,1-d][1,5]pyrimidodiazepine 4 and
5,6-dihydropyrrolo[1,2-f]pteridine 5:
6-[N-Benzyl(2-ethanol)amino]-4-chloro-5-pyrrol- 1-yl-pyrimidine 2a (164
mg, 0.5 mmol) in 6 mL DMSO:DCM (1:1) was treated with TEA (0.703 mL, 5.0
mmol). A solution of SO3-Pyridine (481mg, 3.0 mmol) in 6 mL DMSO:DCM
(1:1) was added, and the mixture was stirred for 35 min at ambient
temperature. The reaction solution was then diluted with DCM (30 mL),
washed twice with 10% citric acid and brine, dried over MgSO4, and
filtered to give crude aldehyde 3a in DCM. To the above solution was
added the amine (aromatic amine 0.6 mmol or aliphatic amine 3.0 mmol) and
TFA(68 µL) (For aliphatic amines, additional 68 µL of TFA was added after
stirring 3 h). The mixture was stirred for corresponding time at ambient
temperature or 40 °C, then washed with saturated aqueous NaHCO3, dried
over MgSO4, and concentrated in vacuo. Purification by flash
chromatography (Petroleum ether/EtOAc = 4:1 or 2:1, v/v) afforded the
desired products.
7-(2-Methylphenylamino)-5-benzyl-1-chloro-6,7-dihydropyrrolo[2,1-d][1,5]
benzodiazepine 4.8a: 86%. mp: 127-128 °C. 1H NMR: δ 8.35 (s, 1H),
7.29-7.21 (m, 5H), 7.02-6.98 (m, 2H), 6.91 (t, 1H,J = 6.9), 6.65 (t, 1H,J
= 7.2), 6.37 (d, 1H,J = 8.1), 6.27 (t, 1H,J = 3.3), 6.16 (t, 1H,J = 1.5),
4.90 (br, 2H,), 4.79 (t, 1H,J = 5.1), 3.83-3.63 (m, 3H), 1.99 (s, 3H);
13C NMR: δ 157.1, 153.7, 153.4, 143.4, 136.6, 133.6, 130.3, 128.8, 127.9,
127.7, 127.1, 124.3, 122.7, 118.3, 116.8, 110.8, 109.1, 105.4, 57.7,
55.0, 48.9, 17.3; MS (ESI): m/z 416.1 [M+H+].
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Parikh-Doering oxidation (stage 1), Pictet-Spengler cyclization (stage 2)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
