mixture was irradiated in microwave reactor (180W) for 20 min at 150 °C.
After completion of the reaction, solvent was removed by evaporation in
vacuo and the crude product was purified by flash column chromatography
on silica gel using ethylacetate/hexane (1:2) as eluent to furnish
7,7-diethyl-2-(2-methylpropyl)-6,7-dihydroindolo[1,2-a]pyrazino[2,3-g]quinoxalin-3(4H)-one
7c (0.082 g, 63%).
6,6-dimethyl-11-(1-methylpropyl)-1,2,6,7-tetrahydroindolo[1',7':1,7,6][1,4]diazepino[2,3-g]quinoxalin-10(9H)-one
(8a) 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ 12.45 (bs, 1H), 7.21 (s, 1H), 7.08-7.00
(m, 2H), 6.72 (m, 1H), 6.71 (s, 1H), 4.15-4.05 (m, 3H), 3.53 (m, 1H),
3.20 (m, 2H), 1.98 (m, 1H), 1.69 (m, 1H), 1.57 (s, 6H), 1.35 (d, J = 6.8
Hz, 3H), 1.01 (t, J = 7.4 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ 162.1,
156.8, 143.8, 140.6, 135.7, 132.0, 130.4, 129.7, 125.2, 124.2, 123.9,
119.0, 113.2, 107.0, 57.4, 52.8, 37.2, 32.0 (2C), 28.3, 27.8, 18.6, 12.6;
MS (ESI): m/z 375 (MH+); HRMS (ESI): calcd for C23H27N4O: m/z 375.2185;
Found 375.2182; IR (neat): 3352, 2961, 1645, 1513, 1429 cm-1.
