$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: To a solution of compound 5a (0.108 g, 0.33
mmol) in CHCl3 (2 mL), 3-pentanone (1.5 equiv., 53 μL, 0.5 mmol) and 2
drops of trifluoroacetic acid (TFA) were added. Upon the addition of TFA
a faint yellow solution turned to dark red color. The resulting reaction
mixture was irradiated in microwave reactor (180W) for 20 min at 150 °C.
After completion of the reaction, solvent was removed by evaporation in
vacuo and the crude product was purified by flash column chromatography
on silica gel using ethylacetate/hexane (1:2) as eluent to furnish
7,7-diethyl-2-(2-methylpropyl)-6,7-dihydroindolo[1,2-a]pyrazino[2,3-g]quinoxalin-3(4H)-one
7c (0.082 g, 63%).
11'-(2-methylpropyl)-1',2'-dihydro-7'H-spiro[cyclohexane-1,6'-indolo[1',7':1,7,6][1,4]diazepino[2,3-g]quinoxalin]-10'(9'H)-one
(8o) 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ 12.44 (bs, 1H), 7.16 (s, 1H), 7.10 (d, J
= 7.8 Hz, 1H), 7.05 (d, J = 7.1 Hz, 1H), 6.73 (m, 2H), 4.57 (bs, 1H),
4.09 (t, J = 8.6 Hz, 2H), 3.19 (t, J = 8.6 Hz, 2H), 2.88 (d, J = 7.2 Hz,
2H), 2.38 (m, 1H), 2.00-1.75 (m, 4H), 1.75-1.50 (m, 4H), 1.48-1.20 (m,
2H), 1.08 (d, J = 6.6 Hz, 6H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ 157.7, 157.2,
144.3, 139.6, 136.0, 132.0, 131.0, 130.1, 125.3, 123.9, 123.1, 119.1,
112.9, 106.6, 58.5, 52.8, 42.6, 36.6 (2C), 28.0, 27.7, 25.5, 23.2 (2C),
22.0 (2C); MS (ESI): m/z 415 (MH+); HRMS (ESI): calcd for C26H31N4O: m/z
415.2498; Found 415.2499; IR (neat): 3358, 2925, 1652, 1517, 1431 cm-1.
