$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 9-Benzyl-2-(2-methoxycarbonylethyl)-1-methyl-2,3,4,9-tetrahydro-1H-β-carboline-1-carboxylic
acid methyl ester (13). To a solution of 12 (294 mg, 0.874 mmol) in dry
benzene (25 mL) were added methyl pyruvate (0.13 mL, 1.4 mmol) and TFA
(67 μL, 0.87 mmol). The mixture was heated at reflux for 43 h, cooled to
room temperature, neutralized with saturated aqueous NaHCO3 solution, and
extracted with CH2Cl2. The combined organic layers were dried over
Na2SO4, filtered, and concentrated to give a residue, which was
chromatographed on silica gel (hexanes/EtOAc, 5:1) to provide 13 (309 mg)
as a yellow oil.
9-Benzyl-2-(2-methoxycarbonylethyl)-1-methyl-2,3,4,9-tetrahydro-1H-β-carboline-1-carboxylic
acid methyl ester (13), yield 84%. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz) δ 1.59 (s, 3H,
CH3), 2.52-2.65(m, 3H), 2.87-2.97 (m, 4H), 3.09-3.20 (m, 1H), 3.28 (s,
3H), 3.82 (s, 3H), 5.27 (s, 2H), 6.81 (d, J = 7.8Hz, 2H), 6.98-7.01 (m,
1H), 7.08-7.11 (m, 2H), 7.17-7.21 (m, 3H), 7.54-7.57 (m, 1H); 13C
NMR(CDCl3, 75 MHz) δ 20.9, 22.0, 34.3, 44.2, 46.1, 47.1, 51.5, 51.8,
63.8, 109.8, 110.2, 118.4, 119.4,122.0, 125.8, 126.4, 126.9, 128.4,
135.4, 137.3, 137.6, 172.6, 173.7. IR (KBr) ν 2949, 1728, 1466, 1238, 741
cm-1; MS (EI) 420 (M+, 0.8), 361 (100), 270 (14). HRMS (MALDI) Calcd. For
C25H28N2O4Na (M + Na)+ 443.1941. Found: 443.1942.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM key step; last stage neutralization; Pictet-Spengler cyclization
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Facile Construction of the Pentacyclic Framework of Subincanadine B.
Synthesis of 20-Deethylenylated Subincanadine B and
19,20-Dihydrosubincanadine B
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
