$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: To a solution of compound 5a (0.108 g, 0.33
mmol) in CHCl3 (2 mL), 3-pentanone (1.5 equiv., 53 μL, 0.5 mmol) and 2
drops of trifluoroacetic acid (TFA) were added. Upon the addition of TFA
a faint yellow solution turned to dark red color. The resulting reaction
mixture was irradiated in microwave reactor (180W) for 20 min at 150 °C.
After completion of the reaction, solvent was removed by evaporation in
vacuo and the crude product was purified by flash column chromatography
on silica gel using ethylacetate/hexane (1:2) as eluent to furnish
7,7-diethyl-2-(2-methylpropyl)-6,7-dihydroindolo[1,2-a]pyrazino[2,3-g]quinoxalin-3(4H)-one
7c (0.082 g, 63%).
7-methyl-2-(1-methylethyl)-7-pentyl-6,7-dihydroindolo[1,2-a]pyrazino[2,3-g]quinoxalin-3(4H)-one
(7k) 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ 12.70 (bs, 1H), 8.31 (s, 1H), 8.20 (d, J
= 8.1 Hz, 1H), 7.68 (d, J = 7.4 Hz, 1H), 7.40 (t, J = 8.1 Hz, 1H), 7.24
(t, J = 7.4 Hz, 1H), 6.87 (s, 1H), 6.42 (s, 1H), 4.59 (bs, 1H), 3.69
(sept, J = 6.6 Hz, 1H), 1.78 (m, 2H), 1.63 (s, 3H), 1.42 (d, J = 6.6 Hz,
3H), 1.41 (d, J = 6.6 Hz, 3H), 1.32 (m, 2H), 1.20-1.07 (m, 4H), 0.83 (t,
J = 7.0 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ 161.2, 156.9, 141.6, 139.5,
134.4, 130.1, 129.0, 127.7, 124.7, 123.0, 121.6, 121.3, 115.7, 112.4,
100.2, 98.4, 55.2, 41.8, 32.4, 30.7, 27.0, 24.4, 22.9, 20.9, 14.4, 14.3;
MS (ESI): m/z 415 (MH+); HRMS (ESI): calcd for C26H31N4O: m/z 415.2498;
Found 415.2495; IR (neat): 3302, 2958, 1651, 1628, 1512, 1453 cm-1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
