$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Amine 32: The solution of ketone 29 (12 mg, 0.027 mmol) and amine 30 (25
mg 0.16 mmol) in dry EtOH (1 ml) was stirred at rt under Argon, and dry
silica gel was added. The suspension was stirred at rt for over 19 hours.
The mixture was diluted with hexanes and filtrated through a Celite pad.
After concentration, the residue was purified by column chromatography on
SiO2 to afford the product 32 (13.5 mg, 82%) as a yellow oil. 1H-NMR
[500MHz, CDCl3] δ 6.52 (s, 1H), 6.31 (s, 1H), 6.02 (s, 1H), 5.92 (s, 1H),
5.62 (d, J= 11.1 Hz, 1H), 5.44 (s, 1H), 4.99 (m, 2H), 3.75 (s, 3H), 3.58
(s, 3H), 3.21-3.14 (m, 2H), 2.90 (m, 2H), 2.65-2.42 (m, 4H), 2.20 (s,
3H), 1.51 (m, 9H); 13C-NMR [75MHz, CDCl3] δ 172.6, 157.0, 152.4, 146.8,
145.0, 144.8, 139.5, 130.4, 125.8, 119.5, 115.5, 114.8, 112.5, 109.9,
102.1, 81.3, 66.5, 64.6, 61.4, 60.8, 55.3, 53.0, 48.3, 47.9, 43.2, 40.1,
37.9, 29.8, 28.9, 21.4, 17.1, 14.6, 9.9; [α]D20 = -51.0° (c = 1.00,
CHCl3); FTIR [neat, υ max, cm-1] 3300, 2900, 1710, 1660, 1490, 740; HRMS
(FAB) calcd for [M+H]+ 601.2220, found 601.2242.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, silica gel used, Pictet-Spengler reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Studies Directed to the Total Synthesis of ET 743 and Analogues Thereof:
