$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: To a solution of compound 5a (0.108 g, 0.33
mmol) in CHCl3 (2 mL), 3-pentanone (1.5 equiv., 53 μL, 0.5 mmol) and 2
drops of trifluoroacetic acid (TFA) were added. Upon the addition of TFA
a faint yellow solution turned to dark red color. The resulting reaction
mixture was irradiated in microwave reactor (180W) for 20 min at 150 °C.
After completion of the reaction, solvent was removed by evaporation in
vacuo and the crude product was purified by flash column chromatography
on silica gel using ethylacetate/hexane (1:2) as eluent to furnish
7,7-diethyl-2-(2-methylpropyl)-6,7-dihydroindolo[1,2-a]pyrazino[2,3-g]quinoxalin-3(4H)-one
7c (0.082 g, 63%).
11'-(1-methylpropyl)-1',2'-dihydro-7'H-spiro[cyclopentane-1,6'-indolo[1',7':1,7,6][1,4]diazepino[2,3-g]quinoxalin]-10'(9'H)-one
(8n) 1H NMR (300 MHz, Acetone-d6): δ 10.81 (bs, 1H), 7.11 (s, 1H), 7.04
(d, J = 7.0 Hz, 1H), 7.01 (d, J = 7.0 Hz, 1H), 6.84 (s, 1H), 6.64 (t, J =
7.0 Hz, 1H), 5.01 (bs, 1H), 4.09 (t, J = 7.5 Hz, 2H), 3.35 (m, 1H), 3.17
(t, J = 7.5 Hz, 2H), 2.09-1.82 (m, 9H), 1.56 (m, 1H), 1.23 (d, J = 6.9
Hz, 3H), 0.92 (t, J = 7.4 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ 161.9,
156.6, 144.5, 140.5, 135.8, 131.8, 130.5, 128.1, 125.0, 123.8, 123.6,
119.0, 113.3, 106.7, 68.8, 52.8, 40.6, 40.5, 37.5, 28.2, 27.8, 23.6 (2C),
18.5, 12.6; MS (ESI): m/z 401 (MH+); HRMS (ESI): calcd for C25H29N4O: m/z
401.2341; Found 401.2339; IR (neat): 3373, 2959, 1663, 1514, 1435 cm-1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
