$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
8,9-Dimethoxy-6,11,12,14-tetrahydrobenzo[4,5][1,2]diazepino[7,1-b]quinazolin-14-ones,
2a-t, 3a-e (General Method). A. A mixture of the corresponding amino
derivative 1a,b (2.5 mmol) and an aldehyde (2.5 mmol) in trifluoroacetic
acid (4 ml) was boiled for 7-8 h. The reaction mixture was cooled,
diluted with water and neutralized with 10% aqueous ammonia to a weakly
alkaline reaction. The mixture was kept for 1 h, the crystals were
filtered off and washed with water. They were recrystallized from acetone
or a DMF-aceto-nitrile mixture. Compound 2o was purified by
recrystallization from 2-propanol or acetone. Compound 2n, yield 80%.
Empirical formula: C24H20BrN3O3; Found, %: C 60.01, H 4.07, Hal 16.60, N
8.89; Calculated, %: C 60.26, H 4.21, Hal 16.70, N 8.78. mp, °C: 211-212.
Chemical shifts, δ, ppm. (J, Hz): 3.55 and 3.87 (6H, s, 8- and 9-OCH3);
4.10 and 4.80 (2H, br. s, CH2); 5.50 (1H, s, CH); 6.30 (1H, s, H-7); 6.94
(1H, s, H-10); 6.90 (1H, br. s, NH); 7.15-7.30 (4H, m, H-2',4',5',6');
7.42 (1H, t, J = 7.6, H-2); 7.58 (1H, d, J = 7.6, H-4); 7.72 (1H, t, J =
7.6, H-3); 8.01 (1H, d, J = 7.6, H-1).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, Pictet-Spengler reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM The Pictet-Spengler reaction in the synthesis of condensed
benzodiazepines 1. synthesis of
6,11,12,14-tetrahydrobenzo-[4,5][1,2]diazepino[7,1-b]quinazolin-14-ones
