$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: To a solution of compound 5a (0.108 g, 0.33
mmol) in CHCl3 (2 mL), 3-pentanone (1.5 equiv., 53 μL, 0.5 mmol) and 2
drops of trifluoroacetic acid (TFA) were added. Upon the addition of TFA
a faint yellow solution turned to dark red color. The resulting reaction
mixture was irradiated in microwave reactor (180W) for 20 min at 150 °C.
After completion of the reaction, solvent was removed by evaporation in
vacuo and the crude product was purified by flash column chromatography
on silica gel using ethylacetate/hexane (1:2) as eluent to furnish
7,7-diethyl-2-(2-methylpropyl)-6,7-dihydroindolo[1,2-a]pyrazino[2,3-g]quinoxalin-3(4H)-one
7c (0.082 g, 63%).
11-benzyl-6-methyl-6-pentyl-1,2,6,7-tetrahydroindolo[1',7':1,7,6][1,4]diazepino[2,3-g]quinoxalin-10(9H)-one
(8d) 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ 12.82 (bs, 1H), 7.52 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H),
7.33 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H), 7.24 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 1H), 7.17 (s, 1H), 7.07
(d, J = 7.4 Hz, 1H), 6.98 (d, J = 7.4 Hz, 1H), 6.75(t, J = 7.4 Hz, 1H),
6.56 (s, 1H), 4.34 (s, 2H), 4.15-4.02 (m, 3H), 3.20 (t, J = 8.1 Hz, 2H),
1.90 (m, 1H), 1.62 (m, 1H), 1.57 (s, 3H), 1.47-1.10 (m, 6H), 0.81 (t, J =
7.1 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ 157.0, 156.2, 143.9, 140.9,
138.5, 135.8, 132.1, 130.2, 129.8 (2C), 128.8 (2C), 128.3, 126.8, 125.8,
125.1, 123.8, 119.0, 113.0, 106.8, 60.2, 52.8, 44.0, 40.3, 32.5, 30.0,
27.8, 24.1, 22.9, 14.4; MS (ESI): m/z 465 (MH+); HRMS (ESI): calcd for
C30H33N4O: m/z 465.2654; Found 465.2652; IR(neat): 3333, 2930, 1652,
1516, 1432 cm-1.
