$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a solution of compound 6a (0.1 g, 0.3 mmol) in CHCl3 (2 mL),
3-pentanone (1.5 equiv., 46 μL, 0.45 mmol) and 2 drops of trifluoroacetic
acid (TFA) were added. As observed earlier, a similar color change from
faint yellow solution to dark red was observed with the addition of TFA.
The resulting reaction mixture was irradiated in microwave reactor (180W)
for 20 min at 150 °C. After completion of the reaction, solvent was
removed by evaporation in vacuo and the crude product was purified by
flash column chromatography on silica gel using ethylacetate/hexane (1:2)
as eluent to furnish
6,6-diethyl-11-(2-methylpropyl)-1,2,6,7-tetrahydroindolo
[1',7':1,7,6][1,4]diazepino[2,3-g]quinoxalin-10(9H)-one (8k) (0.086 g,
71%). 6,6-diethyl-11-(2-methylpropyl)-1,2,6,7-tetrahydroindolo
[1',7':1,7,6][1,4]diazepino[2,3-g]quinoxalin-10(9H)-one (8k), yield
(0.086 g, 71%).
